# features/

Cross-screen domain features for ${PROJECT_NAME}. Use this folder for slices
of behaviour that span multiple screens (auth, profile, analytics, etc.).

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

Every feature folder uses the same four subfolders as `screens/`:

| Subfolder | What lives here | File suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/` | Shared feature components | `*.tsx` |
| `hooks/` | Feature hooks | `use*.ts` |
| `services/` | Business logic + API orchestration | `*.service.ts` |
| `types/` | Feature types | `*.types.ts` |

## When to add a feature vs. a screen

- **Screen**: anything reachable via the navigator. Has its own route.
- **Feature**: anything used by multiple screens. No route of its own.

If unsure, start as a screen — promote to a feature later if you find
yourself importing it from a second screen.

